### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@authToken = your_auth_token_here
@productId = product_id_here
@reviewId = review_id_here

### Get all reviews with pagination and filtering
GET {{baseUrl}}/reviews?page=1&limit=10&sort=-createdAt&status=published

# Query parameters:
# page: Page number (default: 1)
# limit: Number of items per page (default: 10)
# sort: Sort field with direction, e.g., -createdAt (newest first)
# status: Filter by status (published, pending, rejected)

### Get reviews for a specific product
GET {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{productId}}/reviews?rating=5&sort=-createdAt

# Query parameters:
# rating: Filter by rating (1-5)
# sort: Sort field with direction
# verified: Set to 'true' to get only verified reviews
# page: Page number
# limit: Number of items per page

### Get review by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}

# Returns a single review object with:
# - rating (1-5)
# - title
# - comment
# - photos
# - product reference
# - user reference
# - helpful/unhelpful counts
# - status
# - verified flag

### Check if user can review a product
GET {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{productId}}/reviews/can-review
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

# Checks if the authenticated user is eligible to review a product.
# Returns eligibility status with:
# - canReview: boolean indicating if user can review the product
# - reason: explanation message
# - hasPurchased: boolean indicating if user has purchased the product
# - hasExistingReview: boolean indicating if user already reviewed the product
# - existingReviewId: ID of existing review (if applicable)
#
# Requirements:
# - User must be authenticated
# - User must have a delivered order containing the product
# - User must not have already reviewed the product

### Create a new review (requires delivered order)
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{productId}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "rating": 5,
  "title": "Amazing product!",
  "comment": "This is one of the best products I've ever purchased. The quality is exceptional.",
  "photos": [
    {
      "url": "https://example.com/review-photo1.jpg",
      "caption": "Product in use"
    }
  ]
  // "variant": "optional_variant_id_if_reviewing_specific_variant"
}

# Only users with a delivered order containing the product (and variant if provided)
# can create a review. Otherwise, the API returns 403.

### Update a review
PUT {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "rating": 4,
  "title": "Updated opinion",
  "comment": "After using this product for a month, I still think it's great but there are a few minor issues I've discovered."
}

### Delete a review (soft delete)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Mark a review as helpful
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}/helpful
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

# This endpoint allows users to mark a review as helpful.
# Each user can only mark a review as helpful once.
# The helpfulCount is incremented when a user marks a review as helpful.

### Mark a review as unhelpful
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}/unhelpful
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

# This endpoint allows users to mark a review as unhelpful.
# Each user can only mark a review as unhelpful once.
# The unhelpfulCount is incremented when a user marks a review as unhelpful.

### Admin: Add a reply to a review
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}/reply
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "content": "Thank you for your feedback. We appreciate your review and are glad you're enjoying the product. If you have any questions, please contact our support team."
}

# Allows admins to add official replies to reviews.
# Each review can have one official reply which can be updated.
# The reply includes information about who posted it and when.

### Admin: Update review status
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "status": "published"           // Options: "published", "pending", "rejected"
}

# Allows admins to change the status of a review
# - published: Visible to all users
# - pending: Under review, not publicly visible
# - rejected: Review violates guidelines, not publicly visible
#
# Note: When a review status changes, the product's rating statistics are
# automatically recalculated to include only published reviews.

### Admin: Mark a review as verified
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

# Allows admins to mark a review as verified purchase.
# Verified reviews indicate that the reviewer actually purchased the product.
# Verification status is shown in the review object and can be used for filtering.
